From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronghua Zeng <ronghuaz@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 23:58:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: enterprise: add WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise support with
 Transition mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add WPA2-Enterprise (802.1X/EAP) support for fullmac drivers and extend
it to WPA3-Enterprise Only and Transition modes.

Introduce supplicant_config_enterprise_network(), a new entry point for
drivers that manage 802.11 auth/assoc directly (e.g. fullmac). It calls
wpas_add_and_config_network() with do_connect=false so wpa_supplicant is
pre-configured before qapi_WLAN_Commit() fires, avoiding a race where
EVENT_ASSOC arrives before the EAP network is registered.

Add WPA3-Enterprise Transition mode (WIFI_WPA3_ENTERPRISE_TRANSITION,
-S 4): mixed deployments where WPA3-capable STAs select AKM5
(WPA-EAP-SHA256) with MFPC=1/MFPR=0 while legacy WPA2-Enterprise
clients continue to associate with AKM1.  Per WPA3 spec §3.3 a
WPA3-capable STA on a Transition AP must negotiate AKM5.

Key changes:
- Add WIFI_WPA3_ENTERPRISE_TRANSITION to enum wifi_wpa3_enterprise_type
  and its display string; update process_cipher_config() to emit
  key_mgmt=WPA-EAP-SHA256 for TRANSITION mode
- Update wpas_key_mgmt_to_zephyr_wpa3_ent() to accept ieee80211w:
  AKM5+MFPR -> ONLY, AKM5+MFPC-only -> TRANSITION
- Relax MFP validation in wifi_shell: TRANSITION accepts OPTIONAL or
  REQUIRED; ONLY/SUITEB still require REQUIRED; add -S bounds check
- Fix optional enterprise credential handling: client cert/key,
  phase-2 cert/key, anonymous_identity, and key_passwd are now each
  guarded by a length check (PEAP/MSCHAPv2 needs no client cert)
- Fix EAP-TTLS phase-2 method string: "autheap=MSCHAPV2" (not "auth=")
- Fix default eap_ver initialisation to 0 in __wifi_args_to_params()
- Move wifi_enterprise_cert_sec_tags enum into the public wifi_certs.h
  header; add public declarations for wifi_load_certs_from_fs(),
  wifi_list_certs(), and wifi_clear_certs()
- Extend process_certificates() to treat -ENOENT as optional credential
- Add wifi load_certs shell subcommand (CONFIG_WIFI_SHELL_RUNTIME_CERTIFICATES
  + CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_LITTLEFS) with getopt_long parsing
- Fix EVENT_EAPOL_RX memory leak in supp_main.c
- Add ETH_P_EAPOL to packet socket supported protocol list
- Conditionalise optional hostap crypto sources in CMakeLists.txt

Change-Id: I1f5d7ea0ee375aaf9eeee50f960d5eafee3d4e89
